//!
//! # Syscall
//!
//! System calls from ring 3: the dispatcher and the handlers of each ABI.
//!
//! ## Overview
//!
//! The only ABI so far is Linux x86_64, so a static ELF program built for
//! Linux can run. Dispatch is two steps: the ABI of the calling process turns
//! the call number into a kernel operation, and the kernel runs the operation.
//! Adding another ABI means adding a table next to `linux/` that maps its
//! numbers to the same operations.
//!
//! Every pointer a process passes is checked before the kernel touches it
//! (see `linux/write.ign`). A refused range is `-EFAULT`.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name                  | File            | Purpose                                            |
//! |-----------------------|-----------------|----------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Syscall::initialize` | `dispatch.ign`  | fills the Linux table                              |
//! | `Syscall::dispatch`   | `dispatch.ign`  | called by `usermode_asm.S` for every `SYSCALL`     |
//! | `Syscall::Operation`  | `operation.ign` | the ABI independent operations and the table size  |
//! | `Syscall::Linux`      | `linux/*.ign`   | numbers, errno values, the table and the handlers  |
//!
//! The Linux files: `table.ign` (numbers and the table), `errno.ign` (errno
//! values and `failure`), `write.ign` and `nanosleep.ign` (the handlers).
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports   | Why                                                              |
//! |-----------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Proc`    | the current process, its ABI and address space, `exit`           |
//! | `Sched`   | `yield` and `sleep`                                              |
//! | `Mm`      | checked copies to and from user memory                           |
//! | `Time`    | the tick rate that `nanosleep` rounds to                         |
//! | `Arch`    | the `Arch::InterruptFrame` the entry stub builds                 |
//! | `Drivers` | `write` prints on the console                                    |
//!
//! `main` calls `Syscall::initialize`. The assembly entry stub in
//! `arch/x86_64/usermode_asm.S` calls `dispatch` and `badReturn` by their
//! `@externName` symbols, so this facade has to be imported or they are never
//! compiled.

import _ from "./dispatch";
import _ from "./linux/errno";
import _ from "./linux/nanosleep";
import _ from "./linux/table";
import _ from "./linux/write";
import _ from "./operation";

/// Aggregate namespace of the system call code. `dispatch.ign` adds the
/// dispatcher and `operation.ign` and `linux/*.ign` add `Syscall::Operation`
/// and `Syscall::Linux`.
export namespace Syscall {}
